            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Alternative polyadenylation often regulates mRNA isoform usage. In this issue of Neuron, Hwang et al. (2017) describe a powerful new cell-type-specific methodology, cTag-PAPERCLIP, which can be used to study alternative polyadenylation in the CNS.</AbstractText>
